.TH ASTERCTL-BLOB-READ 1 "2026-10-15" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-blob-read \- read an authenticated Aster Blob to a new local file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B blob-read
.BI \-\-id " ID"
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asterctl blob-read
streams a Blob from a running Aster agent into a newly created local file.
It validates contiguous offsets, bounded pages, stable immutable metadata and
TTL, the authenticated completion marker, and the exact declared total length.
.PP
On Linux, bytes are written to an anonymous temporary inode in the pinned
destination directory. After the complete file is synchronized, the command
publishes that exact open inode with an atomic no-replace descriptor link. No
named partial path exists, and closing the descriptor discards an incomplete
read. The command never overwrites an existing or concurrently created
destination.
.PP
The command fails before contacting the agent on non-Linux platforms and when
the destination filesystem cannot create the required anonymous temporary. If
descriptor-link publication is unsupported, finalization fails without
publishing an output path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-id " ID"
Required Blob ID as Base64-encoded 32 bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
Required exact Blob topic.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Required exact Blob scope.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Required destination path. It must not already exist.
.SH OUTPUT
Blob bytes are written only to
.BR \-\-output .
After a complete verified stream, stdout reports Blob ID, publisher, publisher
counter, topic, scope, priority, total length, optional media type, schema ID,
acceptance marker, and original TTL. It never prints Blob plaintext.
.PP
Text renders TTL as exactly
.B TTL: durable
or
.BR "TTL: MILLISECONDS ms" .
Finite JSON uses an exact decimal string in
.BR ttlMs ;
durable JSON omits that field.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The complete verified Blob was written.
.TP
.B 1
Read or local-file handling failed; no partial output is retained.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-blob-publish (1)
